"""Present the exact four-copy N19 AC5 exclusion and cross-catalogue result."""
from pathlib import Path
import html,json,re,hashlib
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;ROOT=HERE.parents[1]
def m(x,display=True):
 tag='div' if display else 'span';return f'<{tag} class="math" data-display="{str(display).lower()}" data-tex="{html.escape(x,quote=True)}"></{tag}>'
def links(items):return '<div class="proof-links">'+''.join(f'<a href="{html.escape(u,quote=True)}">{t} ↗</a>'for u,t in items)+'</div>'
def main():
 r=json.loads((HERE/'independent-verification.json').read_text());assert r['passed'];assert r['certificateSHA256']==hashlib.sha256((HERE/'certificate.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()
 css=re.search(r'<style>(.*?)</style>',(ROOT/'research/t2-qec-upper/index.html').read_text(),re.S).group(1)+'\n.math{max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto}.proof-step{border-left:3px solid #b8c9bd;padding-left:1.2rem;margin:2rem 0}.badge{color:#1c6253;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em}'
 b='<p class="eyebrow">Anticoherent states and subspaces · Exact matrix positivity proof</p><a href="../../index.html#n=19&t=5">← Catalogue entry</a><h1>Nineteen qubits: maximum AC order is four</h1>'
 b+='<div class="result"><span class="badge">Proved · arbitrary complex pure states</span>'+m(r'\boxed{K(19,t)=0\quad(t\ge5),\qquad t_{\max}(19)=4.}')+'<p>A hypothetical fifth-order state would force a strictly positive sum of matrix traces to vanish. An explicit fourth-order state attains the maximum order.</p></div>'
 b+='<section><h2>The four-copy contradiction</h2><p>Average four copies of a hypothetical normalized fifth-order state over collective rotations:</p>'+m(r'X=\int_{\mathrm{SU}(2)}U_g^{\otimes4}(|\psi\rangle\langle\psi|)^{\otimes4}U_g^{\dagger\otimes4}\,dg.')+'<p>This gives a positive trace-one invariant operator on '+m(r'\operatorname{Sym}^4(V_{19/2})',False)+', of dimension 8855. The complete decomposition has 37 spin sectors and 1522 real symmetric multiplicity coordinates.</p>'
 b+='<p>Vanishing multipoles through rank five imply the necessary equations</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{Tr}_1[(T_{\ell0}\otimes I^{\otimes3})X]=0,\qquad\ell=1,\ldots,5.')+'<p>A set of 1380 selected exact physical equations suffices for the certificate. It is not necessary to assume that these equations characterize all possible moments.</p>'
 b+='<p>The rational certificate combines the equations with positive multiplicity matrices. In its explicitly rescaled coordinates, the identity has the form</p>'+m(r'0=\operatorname{Tr}X+\sum_J\operatorname{Tr}(C_J x_J),\qquad C_J\succ0,\quad x_J\succeq0.')+'<p>Here the physical positive multiplicity matrices are rescaled by positive diagonal matrices:</p>'+m(r'x_J=d_J(2J+1)S_JB_JS_J,\qquad d_J>0,\quad S_J\succ0.')+'<p>Every matrix-trace term is nonnegative, whereas the trace of the normalized moment is one. This contradiction excludes every fifth-order state. Taking real parts in the real angular-momentum basis preserves positivity and the selected equations, so the argument also covers arbitrary complex amplitudes.</p></section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Exact verification</h2><p>The independent verifier reconstructs the complete spin representation and the selected contraction equations from physical tensor words. It checks the rational linear identity and all 277 positive pivots by exact rational factorization. Numerical optimization was used to discover the certificate; its numerical status is not a premise of the proof.</p>'+links([('proof.tex','Complete LaTeX proof'),('certificate.json','Rational certificate'),('verify_independently.py','Independent verifier'),('independent-verification.json','Exact verification report')])+'</section>'
 b+='<section><h2>Comparison with the AC-state catalogue</h2><p>The local Liège library and supplied Julia source report a numerical fourth-order state at nineteen qubits, with no fifth- or sixth-order witness. A new five-component radical construction provides exact fourth-order existence. The exclusion above proves its order is globally optimal.</p>'+m(r'\operatorname{supp}\psi=\{0,6,10,14,18\},\qquad \rho_4=I_5/5.')+'<p>The separate sixth-order exclusion is a shorter positive identity involving three-copy total-spin probabilities. Both catalogues show fifth and higher orders as impossible. The separate exact Young-space plane exclusion proves that the maximum dimension at fourth order is one.</p>'+links([('../n19-t4/exclusion/index.html','Exact maximum fourth-order subspace dimension'),('../n19-t4/index.html','Explicit analytical AC4 state'),('../n19-t6/index.html','Independent sixth-order probability proof'),('../../../anticoherent-state-catalogue/index.html#n=19&t=4','Pure AC-state catalogue')])+'</section>'
 head='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>N=19: maximum pure AC order is four</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.css"><script defer src="../../vendor/katex/katex.min.js"></script><style>'+css+'</style><script>document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded",()=>document.querySelectorAll("[data-tex]").forEach(el=>{if(window.katex)el.innerHTML=katex.renderToString(el.dataset.tex,{displayMode:el.dataset.display==="true",throwOnError:false,strict:"ignore",trust:false});}));</script></head><body><main>'
 (HERE/'index.html').write_text(head+b+'</main></body></html>\n')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
